/**
 * @defgroup MIDILAR_Protocol Protocol
 * @ingroup MIDILAR
 * @brief MIDI protocol primitives: channels, groups, masks and data values.
 *
 * - `Channel` and `Group` store the wire value `0-15`, built through
 *   `FromWire()` or `FromNumber()` (SPEC-MIDI-4).
 * - `ChannelMask` and `GroupMask` are sets of the sixteen addresses; Omni is
 *   `ChannelMask::All()` (SPEC-MIDI-5).
 * - `NoteNumber`, `ControllerNumber` and `ProgramNumber` are 7-bit values
 *   (SPEC-MIDI-6).
 * - `Velocity` (16-bit), `ControllerValue`, `PressureValue` and `PitchBend`
 *   (32-bit) keep MIDI 2.0 resolution with a MIDI 1.0 view, converted by
 *   `ScaleUp()` and `ScaleDown()` (SPEC-MIDI-3).
 * - `ToChromaticIndex()`, `ToNoteNumber()` and `ToPitch()` convert between
 *   note numbers and MCC pitches; 60 is C4 and incoming notes are spelled
 *   with an `MCC::Key`, C major by default (SPEC-MIDI-7).
 * - `TimeCode` is an SMPTE time with its MTC quarter-frame encoding
 *   (SPEC-MTC-1).
 * - `Packet` is one Universal MIDI Packet with typed constructors and
 *   queries (SPEC-MIDI-16..19).
 * - `Midi1Parser` turns a MIDI 1.0 byte stream into packets,
 *   `Midi1Encoder` turns packets back into bytes and `SysExAssembler`
 *   collects System Exclusive payloads into a caller buffer
 *   (SPEC-MIDI-8..15).
 * - `DecodeUsbMidi1()` and `UsbMidi1Encoder` convert USB MIDI 1.0 event
 *   packets (SPEC-USB-1..2). Hardware transports live in separate libraries
 *   built on these conversions.
 */

/**
 * @namespace MIDILAR::Protocol
 * @ingroup MIDILAR_Protocol
 * @brief MIDI protocol primitives.
 */
